(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The RTS's semantics of GHC's non-threaded runtime (HE4e; doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md, \"As built: HE4d,"] [10 1 "// HE4e (write-ahead)\"): throwTo blocking its thrower while the target masks (HES41 (a), rts/RaiseAsync.c's throwTo and"] [11 1 "// maybePerformBlockedException), the reachability GHC's collector decides (rts/sm/MarkWeak.c): blocked threads no root"] [12 1 "// reaches resurrected with BlockedIndefinitelyOnMVar, OnSTM or NonTermination (Schedule.c's resurrectThreads), weak"] [13 1 "// pointers whose keys no root reaches finalized (Weak.c's scheduleFinalizers: the C finalizers at once, the Haskell ones"] [14 1 "// by a thread running runFinalizerBatch), at performGC and when every thread is blocked; and the delimited"] [15 1 "// continuations of prompt# and control0# (rts/Continuation.c)."] [17 1 "// throwMsg is a throwTo# waiting for its target to accept it (GHC's MessageThrowTo): queued on the target, its thrower"] [18 1 "// blocked on it."] [26 1 "// ---- throwTo ----"] [28 1 "// accepts reports whether t takes an asynchronous exception now (RaiseAsync.c's throwToMsg by t's state)."] [34 22 "// a blackhole is not interruptible"] [36 16 "// in a foreign call (that called back into Haskell, rtsapi.go; a safe call in flight, threaded.go)"] [38 2 "// an MVar, a delay, STM, a throwTo of its own: interruptible"] [42 1 "// throwTo raises x in t if t accepts it now (true), else queues it on t for src, which must block (false). A finished"] [43 1 "// target takes it as delivered."] [57 1 "// raiseIn raises x in t at once, whatever its masking state (GHC's throwToSingleThreaded): t taken off what it"] [58 1 "// waits on and made runnable at the handler (or ended)."] [63 29 "// a runnable thread is in the run queue already (review 189, L7)"] [70 3 "// a runnable thread, not the one running: its control is its resumption, frozen with its frames (HES56 (b))"] [85 1 "// pendingFor is t's first queued exception it accepts in its state now (maybePerformBlockedException's test), or nil."] [101 1 "// deliverSelf raises the current thread's first acceptable queued exception (at an unmasking, or as it blocks"] [102 1 "// interruptibly while masked interruptibly), its thrower woken; ok false when there is none."] [116 1 "// throwDone wakes a delivered exception's thrower: its throwTo# returns."] [125 1 "// finished wakes the throwers queued on a thread that ended (awakenBlockedExceptionQueue)."] [135 1 "// killThread is killThread# (throwTo): to itself raised at once; to another thread raised when it accepts it, else"] [136 1 "// the thrower blocks, interruptibly, until it does."] [149 1 "// ---- reachability ----"] [151 1 "// gcInfo is what a frame of code keeps alive: the slots its continuation reads and the globals its code names."] [358 1 "// gc decides what GHC's major collection would (MarkWeak.c's stages): the roots (the running and runnable threads,"] [359 1 "// the sleeping ones, the stable pointers, the threads in a foreign call that called back) marked, the weak pointers"] [360 1 "// whose keys are marked keeping their values and finalizers, then the blocked threads still unmarked resurrected"] [361 1 "// (marked: what they reach lives), the weak pointers again, the rest dead. The dead weak pointers are finalized; the resurrected threads, oldest first, get their"] [362 1 "// exceptions. It returns the number of threads resurrected."] [381 2 "// a thread waiting on a descriptor is a root, as a sleeping one (the RTS's blocked_queue)"] [388 2 "// a thread in a foreign call that called back (nested's inForeign) is a root, as GHC's markCapability marks the"] [389 2 "// capability's suspended_ccalls (each InCall's suspended_tso): marked before the blocked threads are decided, so"] [390 2 "// what it reaches (ffi023's MVar its forkIO puts, main blocked on it) is not resurrected (HES83 (a))"] [395 3 "// a thread in a safe foreign call in flight (threaded.go): on the capability's suspended_ccalls too"] [400 2 "// the spark pool (GHC's traverseSparkQueue: sparks are roots)"] [442 2 "// the dead weak pointers, oldest first"] [467 4 "// a thread blocked in throwTo: its target wakes and carries on (resurrectThreads)"] [479 1 "// alive reports a weak pointer's key reachable (a key that is no heap object always is)."] [491 1 "// finalize finalizes dead weak pointers (Weak.c's scheduleFinalizers): each marked dead, its C finalizers run (the"] [492 1 "// last added first), the Haskell finalizers given to one new thread running runFinalizerBatch (which runs the last"] [493 1 "// first: the newest weak pointer's first)."] [516 1 "// runCFins runs a weak pointer's C finalizers, the last added first (runCFinalizers)."] [527 5 "// a finalizer of the program's own C (cprog.go)"] [545 1 "// exitCFins runs the C finalizers of every weak pointer still alive (hs_exit's runAllCFinalizers)."] [554 1 "// lambdaGC is what a closure's code names (its body's and its nested closures' globals), its code compiled first."] [559 19 "// a cycle through the code: its own globals are being collected"] [576 1 "// caseGC is what a case's frame keeps alive: the slots its alternatives read (less those they bind) and the globals"] [577 1 "// they name."] [605 1 "// exprGC is the globals a thread's next expression names."] [702 5 "// the nested closure's code: its globals (its slots are its own frame's)"] [713 1 "// ---- delimited continuations ----"] [715 1 "// Cont is a continuation control0# captured: the frames above its prompt, their slots copied, and the masking state"] [716 1 "// to restore when it resumes (when the frames hold a mask frame: Continuation.c's apply_mask_frame, outer the index"] [717 1 "// of the outermost)."] [725 1 "// contLam is a continuation's code as a function of two arguments (the IO action resumed with, the state token)."] [730 1 "// copyFrames is a copy of frames whose case frames' slots are copies too (a frame sharing slots with another shares"] [731 1 "// the copy)."] [761 3 "// the outermost mask frame now restores the resuming context's state; the captured state applies inside"] [812 3 "// abort to the prompt: the frames and the prompt popped, the masking state the prompt's"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[119 17] [392 36] [396 33] [428 36] [431 35] [522 22] [522 30] [526 28] [556 24] [579 26] [767 35] [788 7] [788 15] [825 37]]} (go/file "rts.go" :imports [


